<div id="alg1.l26" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l26.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">26:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg1.l26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{CE}\leftarrow\text{CrossEntropy}(\text{LLM}(\mathbf{Z}_{S}),\text{Target Labels})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext>CrossEntropy</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mtext>LLM</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mtext>Target Labels</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{CE}\leftarrow\text{CrossEntropy}(\text{LLM}(\mathbf{Z}_{S}),\text{Target Labels})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l27" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l27.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">27:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l27.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Visual Latent Distillation (VLD)
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l28" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l28.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">28:</span></span>
              
              
            Construct <math id="alg1.l28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{A}}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{A}}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> by projecting <math id="alg1.l28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> onto global grid using <math id="alg1.l28.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>.

</div>
<div id="alg1.l29" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l29.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">29:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg1.l29.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{attn}\leftarrow\sum_{i}D_{KL}(\hat{\mathcal{A}}_{T,i}\parallel\text{Softmax}(\mathcal{A}_{S,i}/\tau))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mi>i</mi></msub><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mtext>Softmax</mtext><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒜</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{attn}\leftarrow\sum_{i}D_{KL}(\hat{\mathcal{A}}_{T,i}\parallel\text{Softmax}(\mathcal{A}_{S,i}/\tau))</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l30" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l30.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">30:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg1.l30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{DAC}\leftarrow\lambda_{feat}\cdot\|\mathbf{Z}_{S}-\text{sg}(\mathbf{Z}_{T})\|_{1}+\lambda_{attn}\cdot\mathcal{L}_{attn}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mtext>sg</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{DAC}\leftarrow\lambda_{feat}\cdot\|\mathbf{Z}_{S}-\text{sg}(\mathbf{Z}_{T})\|_{1}+\lambda_{attn}\cdot\mathcal{L}_{attn}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l31" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l31.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">31:</span></span>
              
              
            <math id="alg1.l31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{stage2}\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{CE}+\lambda_{DAC}\cdot\mathcal{L}_{DAC}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{stage2}\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{CE}+\lambda_{DAC}\cdot\mathcal{L}_{DAC}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l32" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l32.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">32:</span></span>
              
              
            Update DAC and LLM using <math id="alg1.l32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\mathcal{L}_{stage2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\mathcal{L}_{stage2}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.3 </span>Algorithm for two-stage training framework</h3>

<div id="A1.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ A.2 Tokenization and Reasoning Formatting ‣ Appendix A Architecture Specifications and Implementation Details ‣ V-Reflection: Transforming MLLMs from Passive Observers to Active Interrogators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> details our two-stage training framework. In Stage 1 (Explicit Grounding Warm-up), the Box-Guided Compression Module (BCM) uses static queries <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> to extract target latent tokens <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{T}</annotation></semantics></math> from localized features <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{F}_{local}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{F}_{local}</annotation></semantics></math>. To prevent representation collapse during alignment, we employ a stochastic decoupled alignment strategy: a Bernoulli indicator <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{I}\sim\text{Bernoulli}(0.5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝕀</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mtext>Bernoulli</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0.5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{I}\sim\text{Bernoulli}(0.5)</annotation></semantics></math> directs the gradient flow via the stop-gradient operator <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{sg}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>sg</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{sg}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>, ensuring only one modality updates per iteration. In Stage 2 (Visual Latent Distillation), with the BCM frozen, the Dynamic Autoregressive Compression (DAC) learns to reconstruct the BCM’s targets. It dynamically projects LLM hidden states into queries (<math id="A1.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Q}_{dyn}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Q}_{dyn}</annotation></semantics></math>) to extract student latent tokens <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> from global image features <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{F}_{global}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐅</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{F}_{global}</annotation></semantics></math>. By minimizing the Mean Squared Error (MSE) between the DAC’s predictions <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>S</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{S}</annotation></semantics></math> and explicit spatial targets <math id="A1.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>T</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{T}</annotation></semantics></math>, localized visual expertise is effectively distilled into the model’s autonomous, global reasoning stream.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Ablation studies</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bernoulli probability <math id="A2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> in the Stochastic Decoupled Alignment Strategy.</span> As shown in Table <a href="#A2.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix B Ablation studies ‣ V-Reflection: Transforming MLLMs from Passive Observers to Active Interrogators" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we investigate the impact of <math id="A2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>, the probability governing the Bernoulli distribution formulated in Eq. 2, within our stochastic decoupled alignment strategy. The results exhibit a clear inverted-U trend, with the model achieving its peak performance across all evaluated benchmarks (MMVP: 70.9, HRBench-4K: 71.1, and BLINK: 54.2) when <math id="A2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is set to <math id="A2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.5</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.5</annotation></semantics></math>.. Deviating from this balanced setting toward extreme values, such as <math id="A2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.1</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="A2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, leads to a noticeable performance drop. This degradation suggests that an unbalanced probability overly biases the gradient updates toward either the LLM or the BCM teacher, thereby undermining the mutual feature alignment. Consequently, <math id="A2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=0.5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=0.5</annotation></semantics></math> provides the necessary equilibrium for stable training, effectively maximizing the bidirectional grounding between the visual spatial queries and the latent reasoning manifold.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span><span id="A2.T4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Ablation Study on Bernoulli Probability <math id="A2.T4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> in the Stochastic Decoupled Alignment Strategy.</span></figcaption>
